records.storyText:
Datui is a TUI application I created to make viewing large tabular datasets in Parquet, CSV, and more quick and easy (hive partitioning too). It is also a landing page for your configurable catalog of data, creates exportable charts, has built in data-quality checks, and lets you query and transform with SQL. Try it as a python module to make viewing&#x2F;debugging DataFrames in a terminal session easy.  It&#x27;s built on Polars LazyFrames, so only the rows on screen are read.<p>Additionally, Datui can read custom binary formats (via a toml spec), CAN, FIX, Excel, Arrow, and others.<p>You can install it with pip install datui, brew, winget, package managers, or a curl script.<p>Try opening up public parquet with this:<p><pre><code>  datui s3:&#x2F;&#x2F;noaa-ghcn-pds&#x2F;parquet&#x2F;by_year&#x2F;YEAR=2024&#x2F;
</code></pre>
Which data formats or workflows would you like to be able to inspect?
